<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Redshift: light keeps the wake</h2>
      <p>During a galaxy’s light voyage, expanding space stretches the light’s wavelength toward longer, redder bands. This <b>cosmological redshift</b> is a stretched signal—not dye, smoke, or a red sail.</p>
      <grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item colspan="30" cell-style="subtle">
          <p role="eyebrow">At emission</p>
          <h3>Shorter wavelength</h3>
          <custom-code>
            <style>
              .wake-short { height: 7.2em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
              .wake-short svg { max-width: 100%; }
            </style>
            <div class="wake-short">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 105" width="360" height="105" role="img" aria-label="A tightly spaced light wave">
                <line x1="10" y1="53" x2="350" y2="53" stroke="var(--body-color)" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-dasharray="5 6"/>
                <path d="M10 53 C20 17 30 17 40 53 S60 89 70 53 S90 17 100 53 S120 89 130 53 S150 17 160 53 S180 89 190 53 S210 17 220 53 S240 89 250 53 S270 17 280 53 S300 89 310 53 S330 17 350 53" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent-color)" stroke-width="4"/>
                <circle cx="10" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--warm-color, var(--accent-color))"/>
                <circle cx="350" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--accent-color)"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </custom-code>
          <p font-size="sm">Successive crests begin close together.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="30" cell-style="subtle">
          <p role="eyebrow">After cosmic travel</p>
          <h3>Longer wavelength</h3>
          <custom-code>
            <style>
              .wake-long { height: 7.2em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
              .wake-long svg { max-width: 100%; }
            </style>
            <div class="wake-long">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 105" width="360" height="105" role="img" aria-label="A stretched light wave with wider spacing">
                <line x1="10" y1="53" x2="350" y2="53" stroke="var(--body-color)" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-dasharray="5 6"/>
                <path d="M10 53 C38 12 66 12 94 53 S150 94 178 53 S234 12 262 53 S318 94 350 53" fill="none" stroke="var(--palette-3, var(--accent-color))" stroke-width="4"/>
                <circle cx="10" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--accent-color)"/>
                <circle cx="350" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--palette-3, var(--accent-color))"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </custom-code>
          <p font-size="sm">Expansion increases the crest-to-crest distance.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p font-size="sm">Across distant galaxies, this pattern is evidence that space expanded while their light traveled. Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/mission/hubble/science/science-behind-the-discoveries/hubble-big-bang/">NASA/Hubble · Science Behind the Big Bang</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>